title: $:/plugins/tiddlywiki/hive/hivelink
tags: $:/tags/Macro
caption: hivelink
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

\procedure hivelink(accountId,permlink,label,canonical:"no")
<$reveal type="nomatch" text=<<label>> default="">
<$button class="tc-btn-invisible tc-hivelink" tooltip="Load the post from the Hive blockchain as a tiddler">
<$action-hivelink action="link" author=<<accountId>> permlink=<<permlink>> canonical=<<canonical>>/>
<$text text=<<label>>/>
</$button>
</$reveal>
<$reveal type="match" text=<<label>> default="">
<$button class="tc-btn-invisible tc-hivelink" tooltip="Load the post from the Hive blockchain as a tiddler">
<$action-hivelink action="link" author=<<accountId>> permlink=<<permlink>> canonical=<<canonical>>/>
<$text text=<<permlink>>/>
</$button>
</$reveal>
\end

The `<<hivelink>>` procedure renders a button that is displayed as a hyperlink. Clicking it loads the Hive post at @@accountId/permlink as a tiddler of this wiki. Call it with the account and the permlink of the post:

<<hivelink harvestmoon299 tw5-my-tiddlywikis-37d8cc783005062a>>

or with an explicit label:

<<hivelink harvestmoon299 tw5-my-tiddlywikis-37d8cc783005062a "Getting started">>

* accountId: the account the post belongs to
* permlink: the permlink of the post (or of the root post of the wiki: the replies are loaded with it)
* label: optional label of the link, defaults to the permlink
* canonical: optional, "yes" opens the ''canonical_url'' of the post instead of loading it if the post carries one

* The loaded tiddler carries the tag ''$:/hive/external'', which the publish filter excludes, so that ''Save to Hive'' ignores it.
* If the tiddler is already present then the version of the post is checked (the ''last_update'' attribute of its replies) and the tiddler is only reloaded when the post was updated afterwards.
* The type of the tiddler is guided by the type declared in the ''json_metadata'' of the post; markdown is the default and anything that declares html (mixed html/markdown included) is served as ''text/html''.

